-- title:
--   Local newvectors from a newform span at most a line
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and let $g$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, that is: $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity $a_{mn}=a_ma_n$ for coprime $m,n$, the recursion $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}-p\,a_{p^r}$ at primes $p\nmid M$ and $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}$ at primes $p\mid M$), and for no proper divisor $M'$ of $M$ is there a normalised eigenform of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M')$ whose $\ell$-th coefficient agrees with that of $g$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$. Let $q$ be a prime and let $\Phi$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb{Q}$ which is an adelic lift of $g$: it is left invariant under the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, right invariant under the finite level-one subgroup attached to the ideal $(M)$, and on adelic points whose finite component is trivial and whose archimedean component lies in $\mathrm{GL}_2^{+}(\mathbb{R})$ its value is $(g\mid_2 h_\infty)(i)$. Let $y_1,y_2$ lie in [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) $\Phi$, the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$-translates of $\Phi$, and assume that each of $y_1,y_2$ lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-translates of the distinguished vector $\Phi$ itself, is fixed by every element of the subgroup [`LocalNewvector.padicK1`](def/LocalNewvector_CongruenceSubgroupK1.html#L161) $q$ $v_q(M)$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$, namely `congruenceK1` for the element $q$ of $\mathbb{Z}_q$ and exponent the multiplicity $v_q(M)$ of $q$ in $M$, and is fixed by $\mathrm{centralGL}_q(z)$, the scalar matrix $z$, for every $z\in\mathbb{Q}_q^{\times}$. Then there exist complex numbers $c_1,c_2$, not both zero, with $c_1y_1+c_2y_2=0$; equivalently, the vectors satisfying these conditions span a space of dimension at most one.
--
--   This is the multiplicity-one statement for newvectors at $q$ in the local representation generated by the adelic lift of a newform: the subspace of vectors fixed by $K_1(q^{v_q(M)})$ and by the centre is at most one-dimensional. It feeds into the proof that the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-representation generated by the adelic lift of a newform is irreducible.
